      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 by the Society of Nuclear Medicine and Molecular Imaging, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Os acromiale is an anatomic variant that in rare cases can cause pain. (99m)Tc-methylene diphosphonate bone scintigraphy with SPECT/CT can play an important role in diagnosing this clinical entity. We present a male football player with shoulder pain secondary to a symptomatic os acromiale, and we demonstrate the findings on bone scanning with limited SPECT/CT that diagnosed this important clinical abnormality."
      },
